# deadcode allowlist — functions that `mise run deadcode` reports as unreachable from
# main() but that are kept on purpose. Format: "<file> <FuncName>", one per line; blank
# lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
#
# Entries are either not-yet-integrated foundations (docs/deadcode-process.md bucket 2:
# complete and tested, awaiting the production caller that wires them) or intentional
# exceptions (bucket 3: test-only seams, deferred behavior, platform-specific code). The
# *ForTest entries directly below are test-only seams; each commented block after them
# states why its entries stay. See docs/deadcode-process.md for classifying a finding and
# for when to remove an entry.
#
# Keep this list tiny — a growing allowlist is a smell, not a convenience.
